{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:ricci-curvature","title":"def:ricci-curvature","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.md","line":178,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex#def:ricci-curvature","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex","label":"def:ricci-curvature","line":368,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Ricci curvature and scalar curvature]\n\\label{def:ricci-curvature}\n\n\\uses{def:riemann-curvature-tensor}\n\n\n\n\nThe symmetric \\emph{Ricci tensor} is\n\\[\n  \\Ric(X,Y)=g^{kl}R(X,\\partial_k,Y,\\partial_l)\n  =\\sum_iR(X,e_i,Y,e_i)\n\\]\nin an orthonormal basis $\\{e_i\\}$, and\n$\\Ric=\\Ric_{ij}dx^i\\otimes dx^j$. The \\emph{scalar curvature} is\n\\[\n  R=R_g=\\tr_g\\Ric=g^{ij}\\Ric_{ij}.\n\\]\nThe inequalities $\\Ric\\ge k$ and $\\Ric\\le k$ refer to the eigenvalues\nof the Ricci endomorphism.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Ricci curvature and scalar curvature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a72696363692d637572766174757265\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ariemann-curvature-tensor\">↗ def:riemann-curvature-tensor</a> <p></p>The symmetric <em>Ricci tensor</em> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\Ric (X,Y)=g^{kl}R(X,\\partial _k,Y,\\partial _l) =\\sum _iR(X,e_i,Y,e_i)  \\]\">\\[  \\Ric (X,Y)=g^{kl}R(X,\\partial _k,Y,\\partial _l) =\\sum _iR(X,e_i,Y,e_i)  \\]</span> in an orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ e_i\\} $\">$\\{ e_i\\} $</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric =\\Ric _{ij}dx^i\\otimes dx^j$\">$\\Ric =\\Ric _{ij}dx^i\\otimes dx^j$</span>. The <em>scalar curvature</em> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  R=R_g=\\tr _g\\Ric =g^{ij}\\Ric _{ij}.  \\]\">\\[  R=R_g=\\tr _g\\Ric =g^{ij}\\Ric _{ij}.  \\]</span> The inequalities <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge k$\">$\\Ric \\ge k$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\le k$\">$\\Ric \\le k$</span> refer to the eigenvalues of the Ricci endomorphism. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:curvature-operator-norm","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:ricci-trace-curvature-operator","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor","title":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor","label":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:ricci-trace-curvature-operator","title":"lem:ricci-trace-curvature-operator","label":"lem:ricci-trace-curvature-operator"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:div-ricci-scalar-curvature","title":"lem:div-ricci-scalar-curvature","label":"lem:div-ricci-scalar-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#divRic","title":"divRic","label":"divRic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:laplacian-one-form","title":"lem:laplacian-one-form","label":"lem:laplacian-one-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lapformula","title":"lapformula","label":"lapformula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blu